NOTICE OF MODIFICATION (Apache License 2.0, Section 4(b))
--------------------------------------------------------

Turbo-WinFare Dense targets a different model, a different graphics API and a
different on-disk format from either prior work, and differs substantially
from both. The following changes were made:

  * The engine is C++20 and Vulkan 1.3 compute, not Swift/Metal (the original
    work) and not Direct3D 12 (the intermediate Windows port). GPU kernels are
    written in HLSL and compiled to SPIR-V with DXC. No Swift source from the
    original work is copied or included in this repository.
  * The target model is Gemma 4 31B Dense, not the 26B-A4B mixture-of-experts
    model. There are no experts, no router and no expert streaming; what is
    streamed here are dense transformer layers. Gemma 4 E2B is supported as a
    second architecture and as a speculative draft model.
  * The container format is `.g4dense`, an original single-file format
    documented in docs/G4DENSE_FORMAT.md. It is not the `.gturbo` bundle
    format and is not compatible with it.
  * Forward-pass constants were re-derived from Google's published Gemma 4
    modelling source rather than carried over, after the inherited assumptions
    were found to be wrong for this architecture. docs/ROUND5_REPORT.md
    records what changed and why.
  * Windows/AMD runtime behaviour specific to this project was added: host
    memory imported through VK_EXT_external_memory_host, a buffered NVMe layer
    streamer on I/O worker threads, a flash-attention (online softmax) kernel,
    and batched speculative verification.

The following aspects trace back to the original work and are derived from it:

  * The MLX affine 4-bit quantization layout (group 64, BF16 scale and bias).
  * The Top-P -> Top-K -> temperature sampling order.
  * The subset of the local OpenAI-compatible HTTP API that the original
    implements, and the CLI flag vocabulary.


